<title>PORTUGAL: PORTUGAL INFLATION ROSE 1.7 PCT YR/YR IN JULY-INE.</title>
<headline>PORTUGAL INFLATION ROSE 1.7 PCT YR/YR IN JULY-INE.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's consumer price index (CPI) was unchanged in July compared with June, while year-on-year it rose 1.7 percent, down from 1.8 percent in June, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was 2.7 percent in July against 2.9 percent in June.</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	 July 97	June 97    July 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise	   Unchanged	 -0.3	  +0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	   +1.7	    +1.8	  +3.8</p>
<p> Average annual inflation   +2.7	    +2.9	  +3.4</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)     133.8	   133.8	 131.6</p>
<p>    Sector breakdown	July 97    June 97	July 96</p>
<p>Food and drink		 -0.2	  -0.9	   +0.2</p>
<p>Clothing and shoes	   -0.2	  -0.2	   +0.1</p>
<p>Health			   +0.5	  +0.4	   +0.1</p>
<p>Transport, communications  +0.3	  +0.1	   +0.1</p>
<p>Education, entertainment   -0.1	Unchanged	+0.1</p>
<p>Tobacco			  +1.2	  +1.5	   +2.3</p>
<p>Other goods and services   +0.4	  +0.0	   +0.1</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
